course: dictionary
lesson: 2657
title: Develop: grow, make or start
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Develop has a few meanings, and the words around it show you which one you need. When something grows and changes over time, it develops. «A tadpole develops into a frog», and a baby develops into a child.
explain: When people make, plan or improve something, they develop it. «In design and technology you develop ideas into products.» To develop an idea means to improve it until it is ready to use.
explain: Develop can also mean to start to have something, like a cold. Photos from old film cameras were developed with chemicals to make the pictures appear. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Develop is a verb: develop, develops, developed, developing.
fact: To develop means to grow and change over time into something bigger, stronger or more complete.
fact: To develop something means to make it, plan it or improve it, like developing skills.
fact: To develop an illness or problem means to start to have it, as in «develop a cold».
fact: Useful phrases: develop into, develop skills, develop an idea.
exercise: «A tadpole develops into a frog.» What does develop mean here? | *To grow and change over time into something new | To lose its tail | To make a new game from scratch | To start to have a sore throat
exercise: Priya says, «I want to develop my reading skills this year.» What does develop mean? | To count them | To lose them | *To improve them over time | To hide them
exercise: «Mia started to develop a cough on Friday.» What does develop mean? | To lend | *To start to have | To get rid of | To finish
test: «Before digital cameras, photos had to be developed with chemicals in a dark room.» What does developed mean here? | To frame them | To shrink them | To send them by post | *To make the pictures appear using chemicals
test: «Ben can't come to school today, he has developed a cold.» What does develop mean here? | To get rid of | To travel to | *To start to have | To forget
exam: «Each cat develops its own meows for its own family.» What does develops mean in this sentence? | *To grow and form over time, learning its own sounds | To hide from people | To meow at dogs | To sleep all day
